 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "In the dining room of Claude Monet, Sasha warmly greets Kostya, Denis, and Max, introduces her fiancé from across the room, and congratulates Max on marrying Vika.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "Костя, привет, как я рада!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Саша, это наш новый повар Денис.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "Привет, Денис, мне очень приятно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Герман Михайлович попросил сделать эспрессо.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "О, Сашка, привет, как дела?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "Всё отлично, я замуж выхожу!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "Вон там стоит мой жених.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Искренне поздравляю тебя со свадьбой!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "Спасибо, я тебя тоже поздравляю.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Лавров, ты чего тут стоишь?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Тебе что, совсем нечем заняться?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Не обязательно торчать тут в зале.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Let's walk through Sasha's reunion with Kostya, Denis, and Max.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "Костя, привет, как я рада!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Kostya, hi, how glad I am!' Sasha spots her old friend behind the bar.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Саша, это наш новый повар Денис.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Sasha, this is our new cook Denis.' Kostya introduces Denis using simple 'this is...'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "Привет, Денис, мне очень приятно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Hi, Denis, very nice to meet you.' Literally 'very pleasant', the universal Russian phrase when being introduced.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Герман Михайлович попросил сделать эспрессо.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'German Mikhailovich asked for an espresso.' When Max walks out of the kitchen, Kostya passes on the chef's order.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "О, Сашка, привет, как дела?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Oh, Sashka, hi, how are things?' Max smiles warmly when he sees his ex-girlfriend.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "Всё отлично, я замуж выхожу!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Everything is great, I am getting married!' For a woman, 'getting married' is 'going out behind a husband' ('zamuzh').",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "Вон там стоит мой жених.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Over there stands my fiancé.' The pointer word 'von' ('yonder / over there') directs Max's eyes across the hall.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Искренне поздравляю тебя со свадьбой!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I sincerely congratulate you on the wedding!' Max offers a polite congratulation.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "Спасибо, я тебя тоже поздравляю.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Thank you, I congratulate you too.' Sasha has heard that Max and Vika finally got married as well.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Лавров, ты чего тут стоишь?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Lavrov, why are you standing around here?' Watching from across the room, Vika marches over to break up their chat.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Тебе что, совсем нечем заняться?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Do you have nothing at all to keep you busy?' Instrumental 'nechem' with the reflexive infinitive means 'nothing to occupy oneself with'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Не обязательно торчать тут в зале.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You do not have to hang around in the dining room.' Colloquial 'torchat' means 'to stick out' or 'to hang around idly'. Now listen to the whole dining room reunion again at natural speed.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "Костя, привет, как я рада!",
   "gap": 0.5
